# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_merge_group.py" "MERGE GROUP GATE: PASS" "merge queue reports overlap or honest Unknown without deadlocking" "merge_group checks_requested resolves and replays the bounded batch, then posts an advisory check on the batch head. An authoritative clear is success; overlap and Unknown are neutral, so none can deadlock the queue. Missing or malformed impact, graph-read failure, incomplete replay, unparseable batch identity, and out-of-window scope are explicitly not analyzed and Unknown rather than false clear. The offline gate covers clear, overlap, every authority failure, malformed payloads, bounded ref parsing, and the manifest subscription." "merge_group always posts a non-blocking batch-head status; only an authoritative clear is success, while overlap or missing authority is neutral" 22
